  "2026-11-05T08:35:31.484Z",codex-agent,"The local full npm coverage attempt was interrupted after existing closeout-workflow fixture failures and is not passing evidence. Isolated first scenario fails on both the branch and disposable pristine origin/main 650797d: real npm ci reports EUSAGE because the synthetic caller has no package-lock, despite its npm shim. The relevant workflow/test are unchanged. Recorded precise reproduction in existing follow-up pm-github-gaq8; no duplicate item created, no out-of-scope code or gate relaxation. CI release gates remain running on c21d40e. Focused 85-case Node/Bun and focused 100/100/100/100 policy coverage remain passing."
  "2026-11-05T08:52:02.249Z",codex-agent,"Review handoff for source c21d40ee5ce23cd80e16db37724657cf5b3b5c46: all three unresolved thread IDs and review-body follow-up are fixed; final complete review-thread refresh found no new threads or newer CodeRabbit review. Six disposable revert proofs are recorded above; restored policy corpus is 85/85 on Node and 85/85 native Bun, with focused policy coverage at exact 100/100/100/100. Full npm run release:check PASSED on Node 26 in CI at 08:46:09 UTC, at unchanged thresholds. At the last observation within the 30-minute cap, npm on Node 22 and both bun run release:check jobs remained in progress: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/41993892442 . These three are pending, not passing evidence; whole npm job also has a later native Bun phase. Job logs are unavailable while jobs run, so no full-suite test total is invented. CodeQL passed at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/41993892315 . Local production audit, package dry run, changelog check and publication attestation all pass; strict tracker health passes with zero warnings. Local full npm attempt remains non-passing due to the independently reproduced main-baseline closeout fixture issue tracked in pm-github-gaq8. No local test/watch process remains. No PM CLI/SDK bug was established in this review. No thread replies/resolutions, mentions, merges, releases, workflow-state changes or secret changes were performed. Releasing only my feature claim; both touched items remain open for orchestrator verification. Final receipt push requires fresh CI and will be reported as pending rather than reusing prior-head approval."
  "2026-11-05T10:25:26.459Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 at 440b830: remote head pulled, origin/main already contained. Retrieved every review thread and all comments; pagination is complete. One unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM6z_gYw concerns stale activation text. Latest review has two outside-diff concerns: GITHUB_TOKEN-generated pushes can park pull_request revocation, and PR-local workflow source can access the merge token before trusted policy loading. Verifying official event semantics, then testing a trusted-base event path with no PR checkout. No replies, resolutions, live configuration changes or merges."
  "2026-11-05T10:30:00.489Z",codex-agent,"Both outside-diff findings are valid. Caller now uses pull_request_target to source all YAML from the trusted default branch and only loads policy from job.workflow_sha. Added independent five-minute/manual audit-only invocation because GITHUB_TOKEN-generated updates can suppress or park PR runs. Audit shares runDependabotMerge provenance decisions, preserves valid armed requests, never arms, paginates all open requests and commits, continues remaining requests after denied revocation, and fails with sanitized errors. README carries full migration template, event-policy requirement and eventual-revocation/server-protection limitation. Official sources: https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/security/securely-using-pull_request_target and https://docs.github.com/en/actions/concepts/security/github_token . No live configuration changes."
